    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. The only test class with `@Test` methods is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are the base class and a log-capture helper), and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the idempotent-create rule for `POST /api/owners`: when a create repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of a duplicate being created (which would otherwise 409).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **New `IdempotencyKeyStore` component** (`src/main/java/.../rest/IdempotencyKeyStore.java`) \u2014 a thread-safe, process-wide map from idempotency key \u2192 created owner id. `record(...)` keeps the first id seen for a key (`putIfAbsent`); `find(...)` looks it up, treating null/blank keys as \"no key supplied.\"\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 before running the create flow, it reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (via `RequestContextHolder`, since the method overrides a generated OpenAPI interface and can't take an extra parameter) and:\n   - If the key was already seen, loads and returns the original owner with `200 OK`.\n   - Otherwise creates the owner as before, records `key \u2192 owner.id`, and returns `201 CREATED`.\n\nThe idempotency check runs *before* the duplicate-identity validation, so a repeat with the same key short-circuits to the original owner rather than tripping the 409 path. A stale key whose owner no longer exists falls through to a normal create (`findOwnerById` \u2192 null \u2192 `Optional.map` yields empty).\n\nBoth responses reuse the existing `ownerResponse(...)` helper, so the repeat returns the identical owner body/`Location` \u2014 differing only in status \u2014 and the test's `assertEquals(id1, id2)` holds.",
