    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of validations and side-effects for `POST /api/owners`, which is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (mapped from `OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER` = `/owners` under the `/api` base). I've labeled each step **[V]** validation or **[SE]** side-effect.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the method body (Spring framework)\n\n1. **[V] Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n2. **[V] Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`), field constraints from `OwnerFieldsDto`:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`: `@Size(1..255)` (when present)\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (when present)\n   - `email`: `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email` (when present)\n\n   (Note: these are the DTO's constraints. The `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` on the `Owner` entity are not applied on this path \u2014 the DTO is what's bound.)\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 `addOwner`: idempotency short-circuit\n\n3. **[SE] Read the `Idempotency-Key` request header** (`currentIdempotencyKey`).\n4. **[V]/[SE] Idempotency replay** \u2014 if that key was previously recorded, the originally created owner is looked up (`clinicService.findOwnerById`) and returned with **200 OK** (with `Location` header and derived fields). No new owner is created; all steps below are skipped.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 `createOwner` (only when not a replay), in this exact order\n\n5. **[SE] `normalizeAddress`** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and flat `address` in place on the DTO; recomposes the flat `address` from the structured lines (preferring `addressLine1`, appending `addressLine2` after a space).\n6. **[V] `rejectBlankOwnerFields`** \u2014 rejects whitespace-only `firstName`, `lastName`, address (neither `addressLine1` nor `address` present), `city`, `telephone` \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400 with `errors` array).\n7. **[V] `rejectDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 rejects an email on the disposable-domain blocklist (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n8. **[SE] Compute `sharesHousehold`** flag from the DTO (`Boolean.TRUE.equals(...)`).\n9. **[V] `rejectInvalidPostcode`** \u2014 when a postcode is present, reject if it's out of range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4 digits) \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` (400).\n10. **[V] `rejectCityAtCapacity`** \u2014 reject if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive count) \u2192 `OwnerCityAtCapacityException` (409).\n11. **[V] `rejectFutureRegistrationDate`** \u2014 reject if the *supplied* `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n12. **[SE] Compute the effective registration date** \u2014 supplied date, else `LocalDate.now()`; then **`businessDay` adjust** by rolling forward off weekends and listed public holidays.\n13. **[V] `rejectDailyRegistrationLimit`** \u2014 reject if that (adjusted) day already holds \u2265 100 owners \u2192 `DailyOwnerRegistrationLimitException` (429).\n14. **[SE] Normalize telephone** to E.164 and set it back on the DTO.\n15. **[SE] Normalize email** (lower-case) and set it back on the DTO.\n16. **[SE] Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; id and pets ignored).\n17. **[SE] Set `registrationDate`** (the adjusted business day) on the owner.\n18. **[SE] Set `customerCode`** \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone+lastName), **deduplicated** against all existing customer codes (reads all owners, appends `-n` on collision).\n19. **[SE] Set `namesakeCount`** \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n20. **[SE] Set `householdId`** \u2014 SHA-256(12-hex) of canonical lastName + postcode, or `null` when no postcode.\n21. **[V] `rejectDuplicateIdentity`** \u2014 reject if the derived identity key (`telephone|email|householdId`) matches any existing **non-deleted** owner \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n22. **[V] `rejectHouseholdDuplicate`** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true (or there's no `householdId`), reject if any existing non-deleted owner shares the same `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409).\n23. **[SE] Set `possibleDuplicateOf`** \u2014 `null` when `sharesHousehold`; otherwise the id of the first existing owner with same lastName+postcode but a different telephone (soft-match), else `null`.\n24. **[SE] Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (assigns the id). This is the primary create side-effect.\n25. **[SE] Set `householdSize`** \u2014 count of owners sharing the `householdId` (now includes the just-saved owner).\n26. **[SE] Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(\"Owner created: ...\")` with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Back in `addOwner`, after `createOwner`\n\n27. **[SE] Record idempotency key** \u2014 `idempotencyKeyStore.record(key, owner.getId())`.\n28. **[SE] Build the response** (`ownerResponse` \u2192 `toOwnerDtoWithDerivedFields`): recomputes `householdSize`, maps to `OwnerDto`, sets derived `bulkSignupWarning`, `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`, adds a `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, and returns **201 CREATED**.\n\n**Key ordering notes:** authorization and DTO bean-validation run first; address normalization happens *before* the blank-field check (so the composed/normalized value is what's checked); the future-date check uses the raw supplied date while the daily-limit check uses the business-day-adjusted date; and the two hard duplicate checks (identity, then household) run *before* persistence, while `householdSize` and the response-only derived fields are computed *after* the save."
  },
